INSERT INTO `posts_translations` VALUES ('en_US',1,'The April Flower Table','A sanctuary for finding peace and the delicate beauty of the plant world. The April Flower Table is a blog dedicated to beauty lovers who seek to understand the meaning, care instructions, and art of floral arrangement to refresh their living spaces. From classic roses to modern houseplants, we have everything you need to \'heal\' your soul with flowers and foliage.','<h2 style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">Minimalist Flower Arrangement&nbsp;</h2><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><h3 style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">1. Focus on Line and Proportion</h3><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">The decisive first step is establishing the composition based on the principle of proportion, specifically the philosophy of asymmetry often found in East Asian art, where the elements <i style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">Heaven – Earth – Man</i> are represented by three main flower stems. To begin, you must select the <b style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><strong>Main Stem (Heaven)</strong></b> – this is the tallest stem, which must establish the dominant line, and its height should typically be about <span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">$1.5$</span> times the height or length of the vase you are using. Next, the <b style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><strong>Secondary Stem (Man)</strong></b> should be trimmed to about <span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">$2/3$</span> the height of the main stem, and the <b style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><strong>Third Stem (Earth)</strong></b> will be the shortest, only about <span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">$1/3$</span> the height of the main stem, used to create stability and balance at the base. Adhering to these proportions from the start not only creates a harmonious framework but also helps the piece escape the monotony of an overly symmetrical arrangement, bringing a more artistic feel.</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><h3 style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">2. The Power of Space and Autonomy</h3><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">The strongest appeal of the minimalist style lies in honoring <b style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><strong>Negative Space</strong></b>. Unlike Western floral styles that often fill every void, here, we must learn to let negative space function as an essential design element equal to the physical object. The goal is to highlight the natural lines of each flower stem, so restrain the urge to overcrowd: use a maximum of 3 to 5 stems. The core principle is to ensure each flower has its own \"breathing room,\" strictly avoiding stems touching, intertwining, or obscuring one another. When arranging, experiment by slightly adjusting the angle—usually 10 to 15 degrees of lean—instead of trying to place them perfectly upright. This slight tilt creates delicacy, subtle movement, and adds depth to your arrangement.</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><h3 style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">3. Highlighting Imperfection and Final Polish</h3><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">&nbsp;</p><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\">Once the composition is set and negative space is established, it\'s time to introduce the <b style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><strong>Focal Point</strong></b> to draw the eye. Seek out unique characteristics: it might be a bud just starting to open, a stem with a slight, irregular curve, or the most vibrant color among your chosen stems. This focal point does not need to be centered; you can place it slightly forward or backward relative to the other two stems to create visual intrigue and depth. Finally, an indispensable step is to rotate the vase 360 degrees. This allows you to perform a final check and adjustment to ensure that your artwork is not only beautiful from one side but also maintains a balanced, harmonious, and captivating composition from any angle the viewer approaches it.</p><p><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/sunset-815270-640.jpg\" alt=\"sunset-815270_640\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"423\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',2,'5 Common Mistakes When Growing Climbing Roses and How to Fix Them','A detailed guide for beginners interested in climbing roses. We highlight common errors that lead to poor growth and minimal flowering, and provide easy-to-apply solutions at home, helping you achieve a gorgeous and robust climbing rose display all year round.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">One of the most common mistakes made by rose growers is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>improper watering, leading to fungal diseases and root rot</strong></b>. Many have a habit of only misting the surface of the leaves or watering in the evening, especially in humid tropical climates, which unintentionally creates an ideal moist environment for fungi such that cause diseases like black spot and powdery mildew to thrive and spread rapidly. To fundamentally solve this issue, the golden rule is to always <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>deep-water the base of the plant</strong></b> to ensure the roots receive sufficient water, and only do so <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>in the early morning</strong></b>. This allows any residual water on the leaves to evaporate completely before nightfall, helping to prevent the growth of mold and protecting the root system.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The second mistake, which is technical but significantly impacts flower productivity, is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>neglecting pruning or using incorrect basic pruning techniques</strong></b>. If growers retain too many thin shoots (suckers), diseased branches, or allow branches to stretch out weakly without shaping, the plant will waste nutrients unnecessarily on parts that do not produce flowers, inhibiting the formation of new flower buds. Therefore, the essential steps are to apply <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>systematic structural pruning</strong></b> (such as creating a Y or T frame for the climbing canes to cling to) and perform <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>heavy pruning</strong></b> (cutting off about <span style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);color:rgb(27,28,29);\"><span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">$1/3$</span> </span>to <span style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);color:rgb(27,28,29);\"><span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">$1/2$</span> </span>of the branch length) after each blooming cycle. This action not only rejuvenates the plant but also stimulates healthy shoots to emerge simultaneously, ensuring a larger flower yield and better flower quality in the subsequent cycle.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The next two mistakes relate to the living environment. The third mistake is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>choosing the wrong growing medium or using pots that do not drain effectively</strong></b>. Soil that is too compact and lacks aeration will suffocate the roots and lead to waterlogging and rot, which is one of the fastest ways to kill a rose. To ensure an ideal root environment, you need to use a <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>loose, nutrient-rich soil mix</strong></b>, which should include amendments like carbonized rice hulls, coco coir, and fully composted cow manure. Furthermore, the bottom of the pot must have large drainage holes and be lined with a layer of material such as gravel or broken pieces of brick to prevent water from accumulating. The fourth mistake is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>insufficient necessary sunlight</strong></b>. Climbing roses are sun-loving plants that require high light intensity; in low light, the plant will exhibit stretching (etiolation), pale leaves, and produce small, lackluster blooms. The ideal planting location must ensure the plant receives a <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>minimum of 6 hours of direct sunlight</strong></b> per day, with morning sun being the best. Finally, <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>neglecting regular pest and disease control</strong></b> is a major flaw. Pests like aphids, thrips, and spider mites can spread very quickly and cause severe damage to buds and young leaves. You need to inspect the undersides of leaves frequently and apply biological pest control treatments (using natural mixtures like soaked garlic, chili, and ginger) regularly, 1-2 times a month, to control the problems immediately, rather than waiting until they reach an outbreak stage.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/huong-dan-trong-hoa-cho-nguoi-moi-bat-dau-copy.jpg\" alt=\"huong-dan-trong-hoa-cho-nguoi-moi-bat-dau-copy\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',3,'The Language of Flowers for Mothers: Subtle Messages Beyond Roses','Explore the profound meaning and cultural origins of flowers specifically designated for Mothers on special occasions. This article helps you move beyond the tradition of roses to select a bouquet that conveys the most sincere, unique, and subtle message, enriching the way you express your filial piety.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_f19dcbc7e343d919\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">To express love, gratitude, and respect for your Mother, there are many floral options that carry subtle messages, extending beyond the typical realm of roses. The first and most symbolic is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Carnation</strong></b>, a flower deeply linked to the history of Mother\'s Day in the US. Carnations are not only a traditional symbol of deep gratitude and a Mother\'s eternal love, but different colors also convey distinct nuances. White carnations represent purity and undying memories, while pink carnations symbolize gratitude and appreciation. Choosing carnations shows an understanding of tradition and genuine respect for your Mother. Another elegant and noble option is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Tulip</strong></b>. With its modern look, minimalist lines, and diverse colors, the Tulip signifies not only thoughtful care and warmth but also represents <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>perfect love</strong></b>, showing absolute reverence for the parent. You might consider colors such as purple (symbolizing royalty and nobility) or pastel shades to create a sophisticated gift.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">If you wish to send a message of optimism, strength, and vibrant vitality, the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Sunflower</strong></b> is an exceptionally suitable choice. This flower, which always turns toward the sun, symbolizes strength, abundant vitality, and reverence, bringing positive energy and wishes for your Mother to always be healthy and cheerful. Sunflowers are often used specifically to honor a Mother\'s resilience. For those who want to give a gift that is valuable, durable, and long-lasting as decoration, the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Phalaenopsis Orchid</strong></b> is a top choice. Phalaenopsis Orchids symbolize luxury, nobility, longevity, and convey wishes for good health, making them highly appropriate for major anniversaries or the Lunar New Year (Tết). Finally, to make the gift unique and multi-layered in meaning, you should consider <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>skillfully combining 2-3 of these flowers</strong></b>. For example, blending the nobility of the Phalaenopsis Orchid with the warmth and sincerity of the Carnation creates a bouquet that is balanced in both aesthetic appeal and emotional message.</p></div><p><br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/88249fdbddcf33f53364341f07cc86c0.jpg\" alt=\"88249fdbddcf33f53364341f07cc86c0\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"650\" height=\"475\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',4,'Tips for Arranging Gorgeous Silk Flowers That Look Just Like Real Ones','A guide on how to transform ordinary silk flowers into soulful works of art that look astonishingly realistic. This is a sustainable and cost-effective solution, keeping your living space fresh without complex care or worries about longevity.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_f18cc9f3d6de5469\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The most crucial secret to making silk flowers look realistic and artistic like fresh flowers begins with the initial step of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>choosing the quality of the flowers</strong></b>. Be resolute in investing in flowers made from silk, fabric, or materials with a natural matte finish, steering clear of hard plastic flowers with glossy paint or overly vibrant, unnatural colors. Selecting details with natural color gradients and clear leaf veins will significantly increase the authenticity. Once you have quality flowers, the technique of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>natural bending and shaping</strong></b> is the next step. Silk flowers are often packaged and stored in a rigid, straight state, losing the necessary softness. You need to gently use your hands to bend the stems, branches, and even the petals, mimicking the spontaneity, soft curves, and natural drape of real flowers to give the arrangement more soul.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">To achieve absolute realism, you can apply the trick of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>using faux water</strong></b> by mixing your own clear glue or resin and pouring a thin layer into the vase. This layer of \"faux water\" creates a powerful visual effect, immediately making the viewer believe the flowers are set in fresh water, eliminating doubt about the material. A small but surprisingly effective tip is to <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>incorporate a few natural leaf details</strong></b> into the silk arrangement. Adding a few available fresh greenery sprigs (such as laurel leaves, betel leaves, or ferns) not only creates vibrancy and genuine green color but also provides a light fragrance, removing the emotional barrier between silk and fresh flowers. Finally, the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>placement of the silk flower vase</strong></b> needs careful consideration. You should place the flowers where there is natural light, ideally near a window or a well-lit area, as the light will enhance the texture of the silk fabric. However, it is essential to avoid direct, harsh sunlight for extended periods, as UV rays will cause the colors to fade and reduce the longevity of the silk flowers over time.</p></div><p><br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/thu-gian-cung-workshop-cam-hoa.jpeg\" alt=\"thu-gian-cung-workshop-cam-hoa\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1500\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',5,'Top 3 Most Reputable Online Flower Markets in Ho Chi Minh City for Busy People','Discover the best online flower shops in Ho Chi Minh City for high-quality blooms and fast delivery. This guide helps busy individuals save time and money while ensuring the perfect gift for any special occasion.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_a36a376e6b39f8fa\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Online flower shopping in Ho Chi Minh City has become the optimal solution, helping busy people easily acquire sophisticated gifts. To assist you in making an informed choice, we evaluated three prominent platforms based on the criteria of Quality, Speed, and Value. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Platform A</strong></b> is rated highest for <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>freshness and premium imported flowers</strong></b>, utilizing a strict cold-chain process from the warehouse to the consumer, ensuring high flower longevity. However, precisely because of its commitment to absolute quality and unique varieties (such as peonies or Ecuadorian roses), their pricing may be higher than average, making it suitable for special personal events or luxury gifts. Meanwhile, <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Platform B</strong></b> excels exceptionally in its <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>lightning-fast delivery service</strong></b> (often committed to completing orders within 1-2 hours) and features modern, youthful designs. This makes it the ideal choice for urgent orders requiring immediate delivery, although their selection of flower varieties may be limited to those that are easy to transport and quick to handle.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Finally, <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Platform C</strong></b> offers a cost-effective and efficient solution for those seeking <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>value and bulk quantity</strong></b>, featuring competitive pricing and frequent attractive promotions. This platform is highly suitable if you need to purchase a large volume of flowers for event decoration, offices, or gifting multiple people simultaneously, although their collection of unique and customized designs may be less extensive than the other two platforms. To make the best decision, you need to consider <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>comprehensive evaluation criteria</strong></b>. Do not just focus on quality and design; you must also factor in the customer service attitude, the professionalism of the packaging (ensuring flowers are not crushed during transit), and especially the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>shipping costs</strong></b> to avoid unforeseen expenses that could significantly increase the total bill.</p></div><p><br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/cho-hoa-sai-gon-6-1630408979.jpg\" alt=\"cho-hoa-sai-gon-6_1630408979\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"700\" height=\"466\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',6,'Utilizing Kitchen Waste as Fertilizer to Stimulate Abundant Flowering','A guide to making organic fertilizer at home using easily accessible ingredients like eggshells, coffee grounds, and banana peels. This green solution helps your flowering plants grow robustly, bloom more profusely, and maintain vibrant colors without the need for toxic chemicals, contributing to environmental protection and cost optimization.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Transforming kitchen waste into valuable nutrients for flowering plants is not only an effective green solution but also significantly helps growers save on the cost of chemical fertilizers. One resource that should not be overlooked is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Eggshells</strong></b>, which contain a very high content of Calcium Carbonate—an essential mineral that helps strengthen plant stems, prevents root rot, and provides stable soil <span style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);color:rgb(27,28,29);\"><span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">$\\text{pH}$</span> </span>. The best way to use them is to rinse the eggshells thoroughly, dry them completely under the sun for sanitization, and then crush them into a fine powder before sprinkling or mixing them into the growing medium. Next is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Coffee Grounds</strong></b>, an excellent source of Nitrogen and magnesium, which helps plants develop healthy, green leaves, especially during the seedling stage. However, coffee grounds are slightly acidic, so they are only suitable for acid-loving plants such as camellias and azaleas; the grounds must be fully dried to avoid attracting insects before application.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Most crucial for the blooming phase are <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Banana Peels</strong></b>, a rich source of Potassium, which is a key nutrient in bud formation, helping flowers bloom larger, more vibrantly colored, and last longer. You can utilize them by cutting the peels into small pieces and burying them directly in the soil near the base of the plant, where they will decompose slowly, or more simply, by soaking the banana peels in water (fermenting them) to create a Potassium-rich solution for watering. This is a natural fertilizer trusted by many flower growers to stimulate blooming. However, the core principle is to strictly adhere to the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Rules of Application and Fertilization Frequency</strong></b>. Even though it is organic fertilizer, misuse or over-application (for example, applying too many coffee grounds which can suddenly acidify the soil) can still harm the plants. Always remember to use moderate amounts, combine a variety of nutrient sources, and gradually increase the frequency of fertilization according to each specific developmental stage and nutrient requirement of each flower type.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/cac-loai-phan-bon-thuong-dung-hien-nay-1.jpg\" alt=\"cac-loai-phan-bon-thuong-dung-hien-nay-1\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"600\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',7,'Reviving Dark Corners: 5 Elegant Flowering Houseplants That Don\'t Need Sun','Discover unique ornamental plants that can still produce beautiful blooms even when placed in low-light areas (such as bathrooms, hallways, or dark corners of the living room). This article helps you bring nature and vibrant colors into every nook and cranny of your home.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_2adb1e9a88ef0454\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Many people mistakenly believe that all flowering plants require direct sunlight, but in fact, there are many ornamental plants that possess beautiful blooms yet thrive well in low-light or artificial light conditions. Introducing these species indoors helps revive dark corners, bringing freshness and color to the space. The first is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Peace Lily</strong></b> (<i style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Spathiphyllum</i>), nicknamed the \"air purifier,\" with its elegant, spoon-shaped white flowers standing out against deep green foliage. The Peace Lily is easy to care for, only requiring moderately moist soil and should be kept away from overly strong air conditioning drafts. The second is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Chinese Evergreen</strong></b> (<i style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Aglaonema</i>); although famous for its diverse leaf colors, some varieties of Chinese Evergreen still produce small, gracefully ivory-white flowers; they tolerate shade well and do not need to be watered too frequently.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Another excellent choice is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Flamingo Flower (Anthurium)</strong></b>. This is a popular houseplant known for its glossy, waxy flowers in red, pink, or white. Anthurium does not require harsh sun, only indirect bright light and high humidity, making it very suitable for placement in a bathroom with a small window. Fourth, we cannot overlook the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Bleeding Heart Vine</strong></b> (<i style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Clerodendrum thomsoniae</i>), a semi-climbing plant with delicate white and red flowers that gently cascade. While it requires better light than the previous three, it still tolerates partial shade and will bloom spectacularly if placed near a north-facing window. Finally, the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Begonia</strong></b>, with many varieties producing tiny, vibrant flowers, is also a wonderful choice. Although it needs some natural light to bloom, Begonias are very sensitive to direct, harsh sun, so a corner of the house with soft, gentle light is the ideal environment for their growth.</p></div><p><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/65363fc837e8f8ed437e1a8b.webp\" alt=\"65363fc837e8f8ed437e1a8b\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"600\" height=\"389\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',8,'Top 5 Sustainable and Cost-Effective Wedding Flower Trends for 2026','An analysis of the latest wedding flower decoration trends, focusing on sustainability (using recycled materials, seasonal flowers) and budget optimization. This helps couples achieve a romantic, impressive wedding that remains environmentally friendly.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">In the context of growing environmental awareness, wedding flower trends for 2026 are shifting strongly towards sustainability and cost optimization. The first trend is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Seasonal and Local Sourcing</strong></b>. Instead of importing expensive, off-season varieties, couples are prioritizing the use of flowers grown locally and in season. This not only reduces transportation costs but also ensures maximum freshness and supports local flower farms. The second trend is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Utilizing Living Plant Arrangements</strong></b>. Instead of using cut flowers, small potted flowering plants (such as blooming succulents, cacti, or herbs) are used to decorate tabletops and can later be gifted to guests as keepsakes. This method completely eliminates floral waste.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The third trend is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Decorating with Dried and Preserved Flowers</strong></b>. Varieties like dried baby\'s breath, pampas grass, or preserved roses are gaining popularity for their unique, antique beauty and their ability to last indefinitely. Using dried flowers significantly reduces the cost associated with fresh blooms, especially in regions with hot climates. The fourth trend is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>\"Less is More\" in Minimalist Tablescaping</strong></b>. Floral designs are becoming more streamlined, focusing on the quality of a few main stems and incorporating more candles, lanterns, or other natural materials (wood, rattan) to highlight the space. The final trend is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Renting Floral Structures</strong></b>. Instead of purchasing flower arches and decorative stands, couples are opting to rent these structures, which cuts down on the cost of raw materials and ensures the items are reused multiple times, aligning with the principles of cost-saving and sustainability.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/rosemixbaby-1024x1024.jpg\" alt=\"RoseMixBaby-1024x1024\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',9,'The Legend of the Tulip: From the Diamond of the East to the First Stock Market Bubble','Explore the chaotic history and thrilling stories of the Tulip – a flower that once triggered one of the world\'s first economic crises (Tulip Mania). This article delves not only into the flower but also into culture and greed.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The Tulip, known today as the symbol of the Netherlands, actually has its historical origins deep within the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Ottoman Empire (modern-day Turkey)</strong></b>. The Tulip was originally called \"Lale\" (in Persian) and was regarded by the Turks as a royal flower, widely used in art, architecture, and poetry. The Tulip was first introduced to Europe around the 16th century. Initially, it was a luxury item reserved only for the nobility and scholars, quickly becoming a symbol of wealth, sophistication, and social status.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">However, the peak of the frenzy arrived in the 17th century in the Netherlands, known as <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Tulip Mania</strong></b>. A viral mutation created Tulip petals with stunning color breaks, which were dubbed \"broken tulips\" (such as the <i style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">Semper Augustus</i> variety). This scarcity and their difficult-to-reproduce beauty transformed them into a type of speculative asset. The price of a single Tulip bulb skyrocketed, at one point equaling the cost of a luxurious house in Amsterdam, or ten times the annual income of a skilled craftsman. This speculative market created a massive \"economic bubble,\" where the price was no longer related to the bulb\'s intrinsic value. The crisis peaked in 1637 when the bubble suddenly burst, causing many investors to lose everything and leading to widespread economic chaos—it is recorded as one of the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>first financial crises</strong></b> of the modern world. Today, the Tulip has returned to its true value, remaining a beautiful flower that symbolizes perfect love.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/nhung-meo-giup-hoa-tulip-hong-luon-tuoi-moi-va-lau.jpg\" alt=\"Nhung-meo-giup-hoa-tulip-hong-luon-tuoi-moi-va-lau\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"782\" height=\"451\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',10,'Edible Flowers: Top 5 Beautiful and Healthy Varieties You Should Try','A comprehensive introduction to the fascinating world of edible flowers that can be used in cuisine and as beautiful dish decoration. The article provides detailed information on their unique flavor profiles, usage, and health benefits, helping you easily elevate your salads, pastries, and beverages.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The culinary world is witnessing the return of edible flowers, which serve not just as decorative elements but also as sources of added flavor and nutrients. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Note that you should only use organically grown flowers that have not been treated with pesticides.</strong></b> The first and most popular varieties are <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Pansies</strong></b> and <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Violets</strong></b>. They boast vibrant colors and a delicate, slightly sweet flavor, often used to garnish pastries, ice cream, or to make decorative ice cubes. Pansies are especially favored for pressing and decorating loaves of bread or biscuits.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Second is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Daylily</strong></b>. Daylily petals have a slightly sweet, crisp texture and are often used in salads or lightly stir-fried dishes. Notably, the daylily buds can be prepared as a vegetable, similar to asparagus. Third is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Carnation</strong></b>. The petals (from organically grown varieties) can be separated and steeped in wine or syrups to create a characteristic slightly spicy, clove-like flavor. However, you must remove the white heel at the base of the petals, as it can taste bitter. Fourth is the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Rose</strong></b>. Organic rose petals can be used to make jam, syrup, or tea. They provide a strong, enchanting aroma and flavor, and are rich in antioxidants. Finally, <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Lavender</strong></b>, with its strong fragrance and herbaceous flavor, is often used in baked goods, making biscuits, or brewing into tea. The most crucial factor when using edible flowers is to <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>clearly distinguish</strong></b> between ornamental flowers and organically grown ones, and ensure that only clean, thoroughly washed petals that have not been chemically treated are used.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/loi-ich-dinh-duong-cua-hoa-an-duoc.jpg\" alt=\"loi-ich-dinh-duong-cua-hoa-an-duoc\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"640\" height=\"640\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',11,'The Secret Power of Chamomile: Detoxification, Relaxation, and Applications in Beauty','Explore the benefits of Chamomile, from promoting sleep and reducing stress to natural beauty recipes. The article introduces effective ways to use fresh and dried chamomile.','<p>Chamomile has long been considered one of the most valuable herbs, renowned for its ability to <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>soothe the nervous system and aid sleep</strong></b>. The compound apigenin found in Chamomile has a mild sedative effect, helping to reduce anxiety and stress. A warm cup of Chamomile tea before bed is an effective natural solution for improving sleep quality. Furthermore, this flower also possesses powerful <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>anti-inflammatory and antioxidant properties</strong></b>. When consumed as tea, it helps soothe minor digestive issues, reduce stomach spasms, and supports the liver detoxification process. In the beauty domain, Chamomile is also a miraculous ingredient. Chamomile essential oil has antibacterial and skin-calming properties, making it very effective in <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>reducing irritation and redness</strong></b> and supporting the treatment of sensitive skin issues or acne. You can use distilled Chamomile water as a skin toner or use spent tea bags as an eye compress to reduce dark circles and puffiness. To maximize the benefits, you should opt for organically grown Chamomile. You can use the fresh flowers for decoration and immediate consumption as a beverage, or dry them for later use, ensuring that the flavor and medicinal properties are optimally preserved.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/cuc-la-ma-1.jpg\" alt=\"cuc-la-ma-1\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"800\" height=\"500\"><br><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',12,'The \"3 Golden Placement Rules\" for Vases to Enhance Prosperity in Your Home','A guide to applying basic principles of Feng Shui and interior design to choose the placement of flower vases, aiming to optimize the aesthetic appeal of the space and attract positive energy, good fortune, and wealth for the homeowner.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">In interior design, a beautiful vase of flowers is not just a decorative item but also a crucial element that influences the flow of energy and the aesthetics of the space. The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>First Golden Placement is the Dining Table</strong></b>. Placing a vibrant, fresh flower arrangement on the dining table helps stimulate appetite and creates a warm, intimate atmosphere for family meals. However, avoid flowers with overly strong fragrances. The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Second Golden Placement is the Entrance Hall/Main Foyer</strong></b>. This area is where energy enters the home; a brightly colored flower arrangement here helps attract positive energy (prosperity/vitality) and creates a strong, welcoming impression. According to Feng Shui, flowers in red, yellow, or purple should be chosen for this spot to activate wealth and luck.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Third Golden Placement is the Workspace or Reading Nook</strong></b>. Placing a small potted flowering plant or a minimalist floral arrangement helps soothe the eyes, reduce stress, and boost concentration. However, it is essential to avoid placing artificial or withered flowers, as they can bring negative energy. As a general rule, you should choose a vase with a size and shape that complements the surrounding furniture; tall vases suit the console table in the foyer, and low, round vases are ideal for coffee or dining tables. Maintaining fresh flowers and regularly changing the water is a prerequisite for the vase to not only look beautiful but also genuinely bring good fortune and prosperity.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/hoa-de-ban-lam-viec-1-768x576-1.jpg\" alt=\"hoa-de-ban-lam-viec-1-768x576-1\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"768\" height=\"576\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',13,'Discover the Ha Giang Buckwheat Flower Fields: Itinerary, Best Season, and Photography Tips','Detailed travel experience sharing for Ha Giang during the Buckwheat Flower season. The article provides information on the peak blooming period, famous viewing spots, and the best photography tips for stunning \"check-in\" photos amidst the vast flower fields.','<p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The Buckwheat Flower (Tam Giác Mạch) has become an inseparable symbol of the Đồng Văn Karst Plateau (Ha Giang), attracting millions of tourists annually. The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>most ideal time</strong></b> to admire this flower is from <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>late October to early December</strong></b>. This is when the flowers are in peak bloom, covering the hillsides in a romantic purplish-pink hue. However, if you visit late in the season, you will have the chance to see the flowers turn into a beautiful deep crimson color. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Famous viewing spots</strong></b> that cannot be missed include Lũng Cú (near the National Flagpole), Sủng Là valley (home to Pao\'s House), and the Mã Pí Lèng Pass area, where the flower fields blend seamlessly with the magnificent rocky mountain scenery.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">To capture the best photos, you need to keep a few <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>photography tips</strong></b> in mind. Take advantage of the <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>early morning light</strong></b> (around 7 AM – 9 AM) when dew still clings to the petals to create a magical effect, or shoot at <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>dusk</strong></b> to capture warm tones. You should choose clothing with colors that strongly contrast with the flowers\' hue (e.g., white, black, or neutral tones) to stand out against the field. Most importantly, when visiting, tourists must be mindful of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>protecting the flower fields</strong></b> by walking on the designated pathways and avoiding causing damage to the local people\'s flowers, thus contributing to the sustainable preservation of this beautiful landscape.<br><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/ngo-ngang-ve-dep-mien-son-cuoc-voi-mua-hoa-tam-gia.jpg\" alt=\"ngo-ngang-ve-dep-mien-son-cuoc-voi-mua-hoa-tam-gia\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1707\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',14,'Scented Soap Flower Gift Box: The Solution for Preserving Eternal Memories (and 3 DIY Methods)','An introduction to the trend of gift boxes featuring scented soap flowers. The article delves into the benefits of soap flowers (longevity, fragrance) and guides you through 3 simple formulas to make your own highly personalized scented soap flower gift box at home.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_58ec470da715bcd2\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Scented soap flower gift boxes are becoming a popular gifting trend due to the combination of the flower\'s aesthetic appeal and its ability to retain fragrance and memories long-term. The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>biggest advantage of soap flowers</strong></b> is their superior longevity (they can retain their shape and color for several years), coupled with their ability to emit a gentle, romantic fragrance, unlike fresh flowers that only last a few days. To make a unique gift box yourself, you can try 3 simple formulas. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Formula 1 (Basic Soap Flowers):</strong></b> Purchase pre-shaped soap flowers, then arrange them in a box (using dry floral foam) and spray an extra layer of essential oil (such as Lavender or Rose) to intensify the aroma.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Formula 2 (Molded Scented Wax - Cold Aromatherapy Wax):</strong></b> Mix melted beeswax or soy wax with essential oils, then pour the mixture into flower or letter-shaped molds. Once the wax is hardened, you can use these wax pieces to decorate and intersperse with silk flowers in the gift box. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Formula 3 (Combined with Dried Botanicals):</strong></b> Mix the soap flowers with dried botanicals that possess natural fragrances, such as cinnamon, star anise, or dried orange peel. This not only enhances the rustic aesthetic but also helps the fragrance last longer and smell more natural. Making a soap flower gift box yourself not only saves costs but also allows the gift to carry a personal touch, demonstrating the giver\'s sincerity.</p></div><p><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/hop-qua-hoa-hong-sap-2-ngan-kem-thiep-10.jpg\" alt=\"hop-qua-hoa-hong-sap-2-ngan-kem-thiep-10\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"700\" height=\"700\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',15,'Hydroponics for Flowering Plants: Minimalist Water-Based Growing Techniques for Modern Spaces','An introduction to water-based flower cultivation techniques (hydroponics) – a clean, modern method suitable for various indoor flowering plants. The article provides detailed instructions on how to select plants, prepare nutrient solutions, and troubleshoot common issues.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_92a3f07fcbad4ecc\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Growing flowers using the hydroponic method has become increasingly popular due to its cleanliness and high aesthetic value, making it highly suitable for modern apartments and workspaces. The greatest benefit is the complete elimination of soil, which helps to <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>prevent pests and bacteria</strong></b> and keeps the living space perpetually clean. This technique focuses on delivering a nutrient solution directly to the plant roots. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Plant selection</strong></b> is crucial; flowering plants suitable for hydroponics include the Peace Lily, Chinese Evergreen, and especially those species with semi-aquatic root systems.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Preparing the nutrient solution</strong></b> is the core step. Plants require essential macro-nutrients (<span style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);color:rgb(27,28,29);\"><span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">$N-P-K$</span> </span>) and micro-nutrients. You can purchase specialized hydroponic solutions readily available on the market, or mix your own with precise dosages to ensure the plant receives all the necessary nutrients for the blooming process. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>The procedure involves:</strong></b> thoroughly cleaning the plant roots of all soil, placing the roots into a container filled with water/solution, and changing the water weekly. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Common issues</strong></b> include the growth of green algae in the container (due to light exposure) or root rot. To fix these problems, you should use dark-colored or opaque containers to limit light contact with the water, and always ensure the roots have ample ventilation and are not fully submerged.<br>&nbsp;</p></div><p><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/gemini-generated-image-o57ghjo57ghjo57g-3.png\" alt=\"Gemini_Generated_Image_o57ghjo57ghjo57g (3)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\"><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',16,'Growing Lavender at Home: From Care to Harvest and Versatile Applications','A detailed guide on how to plant, care for, and harvest Lavender—a flowering herb beloved for its fragrance and relaxing properties. The article includes applications for home beauty and culinary use.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_b3c5bcd09c08b031\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">Lavender is not only famous for its romantic purple fields but is also a versatile herb commonly grown at home. The prerequisite for successfully growing Lavender is <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>providing adequate sunlight</strong></b>. The plant requires at least 6-8 hours of direct sun daily. Regarding soil, Lavender prefers <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>poorly nourished, dry soil with excellent drainage</strong></b>. Soil that is too rich in nutrients or retains too much water will easily cause root rot and kill the plant. You should add sand or gravel to the soil mixture to enhance drainage capabilities.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\"><b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Care techniques</strong></b> include moderate watering (only watering when the soil has completely dried out) and frequent pruning. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Pruning</strong></b> is a crucial step for maintaining the plant\'s shape and encouraging more profuse blooming. After the flowers fade, prune immediately below the flower spikes. <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>Harvesting</strong></b> should be done when the flower buds are just starting to open, cutting them in the early morning after the dew has evaporated. In terms of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>applications</strong></b>, Lavender can be dried to make scented sachets, sleep pillows (for relaxation), or brewed as tea. In cuisine, Lavender is used to make biscuits, ice cream, or as a spice rub for lamb, providing a unique and delicate herbaceous flavor.</p></div><p><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/81eukzqpxjl-ac-uf10001000-ql80.jpg\" alt=\"81euKzQpXjL._AC_UF1000,1000_QL80_\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1000\" height=\"668\"><br><br><br>&nbsp;</p>'),('en_US',17,'The Art of the Natural Hand-Tied Bouquet for the Modern Bride','Explore the \"Wildflower Style\" wedding bouquet—a free-spirited, asymmetrical style that mimics the wild beauty of meadow flowers. The article guides you on how to select flower types, colors, and binding techniques to create a romantic, personalized bridal bouquet.','<div class=\"markdown markdown-main-panel enable-updated-hr-color\" style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" id=\"model-response-message-contentr_8a582e384f7107aa\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">The \"Wildflower Style\" (Natural/Meadow Flower Style) hand-tied bouquet is a leading choice for modern brides who cherish romance, freedom, and individuality. The hallmark of this style is its <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>asymmetry, free-flowing nature</strong></b>, and disregard for rigid, classic rounded forms. Instead of being tightly arranged, the flowers are loosely gathered, featuring varying lengths and degrees of drape, mimicking the spontaneous beauty of flowers freshly picked from a field.</p><p style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px 0px 16px;padding:0px;\">To achieve the \"Wildflower Style\" effect, <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>flower selection</strong></b> is crucial. You should choose a combination of main blooms (such as garden roses, peonies) with delicate, slender, and airy filler flowers (like baby\'s breath, small daisies, or bells of Ireland). Furthermore, the use of <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>draping foliage and green branches</strong></b> (such as silver dollar eucalyptus, cinerea, or cascading vines) is essential to create a natural and expansive texture. Regarding <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>color</strong></b>, this style often favors earthy tones and soft pastels, combined with dark accents to add depth. The <b style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);color:rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\"><strong>binding technique</strong></b> requires skill to ensure the bouquet remains sturdy to hold, despite its seemingly loose structure. The bouquet should be held at a <span style=\"background-color:rgba(0,0,0,0);color:rgb(27,28,29);\"><span class=\"math-inline\" style=\"border:0px none rgb(27,28,29);font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin:0px;padding:0px;\">$45^\\circ$</span> </span>angle, then tightly secured with silk ribbon or lace fabric to complete the rustic, romantic look.</p></div><p style=\"font-family:\'Google Sans Text\', sans-serif;line-height:1.15;margin-top:0px;\"><br><img src=\"https://lylyecogroup.hisotechgroup.vn/storage/gemini-generated-image-9bbjmd9bbjmd9bbj-1.png\" alt=\"Gemini_Generated_Image_9bbjmd9bbjmd9bbj (1)\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\"><br>&nbsp;</p>');
